### `pyproject.toml` Structure for Tools

When creating a project that includes command-line applications, you MUST define them in the `[project.scripts]` table of the `pyproject.toml` file. This makes them runnable via `uv run`.

**Example `pyproject.toml` for a CLI tool:**

```toml
[project]
name = "my-cli-tool"
version = "0.1.0"
dependencies = [
  "click==8.1.7",
]

[project.scripts]
my-cli = "my_cli_tool.main:cli"

[build-system]
requires = ["hatchling"]
build-backend = "hatchling.build"
```
